---
title: Wine Country French Toast
servings: 2
source: http://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/wine-country-french-toast-recipe/index.html
tags: breakfast, alcohol
---

= Roasted Grapes =
Preheat the oven to 325°F.

In a bowl, combine the @seedless red grapes{1%cup}(halved), @grapeseed oil{1/2%tsp},
@dried rosemary{1/4%tsp}, and @kosher salt{pinch}.
Mix to coat the grapes evenly.

Scatter the grapes on a #sheet pan{} or in a large skillet and roast in the oven, ~{15-20%minutes}.
They should not be shriveled up, just plump and juicy.

= Pinot Noir Rosemary Syrup =
In the meantime, in a stainless steel saucepan, add the @pinot noir{1%cup} and @fresh rosemary{1%sprig}.
Simmer on medium-low heat until reduced by half, ~{15-20%minutes}.

Remove the rosemary, add the @maple syrup{1/3%cup}, turn off the heat and let rest.
(This can be done ahead of time.)

= Egg Wash =
In a bowl or #casserole dish{} large enough to fit the bread flatly on the surface,
beat the @eggs{3}, @whole milk{1/4%cup}, @sugar{2%tbsp}, @cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, and @vanilla{1/2%tsp}.
Beat until all the ingredients are well combined.

= French Toast =
Heat a large nonstick or cast-iron #skillet to medium-high.
Dip the @challah bread{2%slices}(1" thick) in egg wash on both sides,
allowing the egg wash to soak in but not over saturate the bread.

Add the @butter{2%tbsp} to the skillet and let melt.
Place the bread in the skillet and let brown, about 3 minutes.

Flip the bread over and place some @French brie{1%wheel}(sliced) on the cooked side of 1 slice of bread.
Allow the cheese to soften while the second side cooks to golden brown.

Turn off the heat and sandwich the 2 slices together.
Cut the bread on a diagonal and plate.
Top with roasted grapes and drizzle with pinot noir syrup.
